ings and exact migration targets; apply the same analyzer to scaffolding, package doctor, CLI, MCP, contracts, and first-party package governance; test the three reported spellings plus negative controls in disposable packages; document compatibility and rollout behavior."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make extension compatibility declarations schema-closed and impossible to mistake for enforced policy."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Package authors receive deterministic diagnostics for misspelled, misplaced, stale, or unsupported compatibility declarations."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Packages can remain green while shipping a version floor that no consumer enforces, causing fleet drift and downstream history incompatibility."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"SDK analyzers, manifests, scaffolds, package doctor, CLI, MCP, and contracts share one strict compatibility-key vocabulary with migration guidance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GitHub #1032 documents three live packages with three spellings and silent green checks."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Current extension manifest SDK and package fleet on 2026-08-15"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Pass manifests containing compatibility.pm, nested pm.pm_min_version, and stale top-level pm_min_version through checkExtensionManifestCompatibility; observe no unknown-key finding and compatible=true for the first two."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Unknown or misplaced compatibility-like keys are diagnosed with a stable typed finding and an executable correction; valid top-level pm_min_version remains enforced across SDK and package surfaces."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Compatibility-looking fields can be ignored silently, so internally consistent packages and tests remain green while no version floor is enforced."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1w0d","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T15:26:48.504Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-15T15:26:48.504Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for GH-1032, manifest unknown key, pm_min_version, compatibility.pm, and nested compatibility found no item for this silent manifest-schema gap. Closed pm-1w0d owns the existing compatibility analyzer and is linked as provenance; this item records the newly reported cross-package validation defect without reopening completed work."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2f72e8341e01b2641664d7bd579d5c3a0ad2b498fa598087ec3a0f78aeacef67","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
